(8) Demand paging steers on a page fault: the fault address is translated into a virtual page via a radix tree of the process address space, the mapping found and its permissions checked before I/O is scheduled. The physical allocator keeps a buddy list per migratetype; when the list drains, compaction moves movable pages toward one end of the zone to coalesce free extents. Swap cache is keyed by backing store index; two mappings of one page collapse to a single swap entry by reference counting the handle. Reference bit propagation approximates LRU: each generation, page access bits are exported, cleared, and their histrogram parks on a spectral histogram, from which reclaim chooses the coldest. Writeback orders pages by dirty time and groups contiguous extents; the flusher wakes when the dirty ratio crosses its threshold and caps the number of submitters so that locality is kept. Translation lookaside buffers use a two-level structure; the second level is physically indexed and tagged by address space identifier, so a context switch invalidates only the fall-through of the per-process generation counter. Huge pages amortize translation cost but must scan a contiguous range; the fault handler falls back to base pages when alignment fails.

